@startuml revoke-and-unbind
!theme plain
title Ending access: grant revocation, task end, account withdrawal

actor "Person / operator" as P
participant "swarma-dispatcher" as D
participant "swarma-user-manager" as H
participant "swarma-credential-broker" as B

== a grant is revoked ==
P -> B: revocation.put (signed revocation envelope, §6.4)
B -> B: verify swarma-credential-broker revocation/1 signature\nunder the state lock: write the new revocation state\n(temp file, flush, rename, flush directory), update memory
B --> P: acknowledged (only after the state is durable)
B -> B: next lease/renewal: lease_grant_revoked for the lease chain,\nlease_caller_revoked for the caller chain (method-specific refusals)

== the task ends ==
D -> B: unbind {binding_id}
B -> B: end the binding's leases; close uid 30412's connections
D -> H: user.retire {generation: g-0193, home: archive}\n(abbreviated helper request; distinct retire effect ID)
H -> H: state retiring: launcher refuses g-0193;\nstop processes, verify quiescence; (v1: egress stays denied)
H -> H: quarantine and archive or delete the home;\nremove account and group; state removed
H --> D: removed
note over D,H: Future keeper integration (D-IDENTITY): after retirement,\ndispatcher separately revokes only identities registered as one-shot.\nStanding identities require a signed operator revocation;\nunbind/retire are not blanket identity revocation.
note over B: a recycled UID or a repeated label inherits nothing:\nbindings, grants and leases are keyed by generation

== the account is withdrawn ==
P -> B: account.revoke {account: owner/claude/personal}
B -> B: delete the material; state revoked; every lease → lease_account_revoked
P -> P: revoke at the vendor (Claude UI or Codex auth-owner logout);\ntokens already copied end only there or at expiry
@enduml
